.title = "Choose your path",
.description = "Choose the ZML framework for model code or LLMD for serving models to applications.",
.date = .date("2026-11-06T00:00:00"),
.layout = "content.shtml",
---
Use the [Compatibility reference]($link.page('reference/compatibility')) to
check the build target or server artifact for your host, accelerator,
checkpoint, and precision.

# [Build with ZML]($heading.id('build-with-zml'))

Choose ZML when you want to write or change model code. The framework handles
tensor operations, weight loading, compilation, and execution.

- [Run MNIST with Bazel]($link.page('zml/quickstart')) to classify a digit on CPU.
- [Write your first model]($link.page('zml/first-model')) to define a tagged
  linear layer and read its output.
- [Build and run with Bazel]($link.page('zml/build-and-run')) to choose an
  accelerator, run an LLM example, or package a build for another host.

# [Serve models with LLMD]($heading.id('serve-models-with-llmd'))

Choose LLMD when you want applications to call a model through an
OpenAI-compatible HTTP API. Start a server yourself or connect to an existing
LLMD endpoint.

- [Start LLMD]($link.page('llmd/quickstart')) with a recipe for your hardware
  and send a chat request.
- [Compare checkpoints]($link.page('llmd/models')) by backend, precision, and
  LLMD release.
- [Connect to an existing endpoint]($link.page('llmd/api')) to list the model,
  send chat requests, or stream responses.
- [Operate an LLMD service]($link.page('operations')) for deployment,
  monitoring, troubleshooting, and rollback.
